# MC-X-F12 (writer 9), a scenario's expression row (L §6.4: "evaluated at the row's keys and law date"; it "reads
# inputs, bands and defs"): k, which the scenario declares, has one row governing always, `hh.rate(3)`, and rate's
# table governs always, so k reads nothing law-dated and r needs no at (L §4.3 rule 2; L §6.4 "A row of an input the
# scenario declares may govern always (it then needs no law date, §4.3)"). rate(3) = 400.00 PLN. snap12: REFCORE-NOT-YET
# (the interpreter guard on every band read with no law date).
=== base.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source act "the act"

band rate(a: int): money PLN

version v_act
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  rate: [0, 6) = 400.00 PLN "under 6"
  rate: [6, 18) = 250.00 PLN "6 to 17"
=== s.tally
scenario s over hh
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

input k: money PLN
def r: money PLN = k

version vs
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  k = hh.rate(3) "linked"

ask q: r in s
=== expect
q: 400.00 PLN
  world: s
  cut 2027-12-31
